 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Light for «بل الله يزكي من يشاء» only. 51:12-20 (their claim that the disbelievers are better guided) is glossed with As-Sa'di's motive (envy), never with the claim itself. 52:5-11 «فلن تجد له نصيرا» gets «وهذا غاية الخذلان», not a positive definition of «نصيرا». No people drawn. STAGING v4: 49-50: a group in a town praises itself (speak on 49:5 and 50:3, inventing lies); light plate for His purifying whom He wills; the Prophet addressed is not shown. 51-52: those given part of the Book (Al-Muyassar: the Jews) turn on 51:10 (believing in idols and tyrants: no idol drawn) then walk over to the disbelievers and speak to them, pointing at them on 51:15 (a conversation, not two crowds facing off) (their claim, glossed only with As-Sa'di's motive); the believers they disparage are not drawn. Nobody fades on the curse (52:3-7)."
